alidity by file on current origin/main before edits:\n- docs/env-vars.md: no retired-spelling hits; generated env docs already omitted old aliases.\n- docs/config-reference.md: only canonical verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets row; no verify.overlap_enabled.\n- tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py: no retired-spelling hits.\n- tests/golden/config_surface.json: canonical config/env entries only; old COMPACT_THRESHOLD/SCRATCH_BASE_DIR hits are substrings of REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD/REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR.\n- docs/api-stability.md: already aligned before this change; lines 27 and 33-34 cite ADR 0116 and the pre-1.0 operator-approved clean-removal exception.\n- docs/config.md, docs/bash-migration.md, docs/concurrency.md, docs/release-notes.md, CHANGELOG.md had remaining stale/live-alias publication gaps and were fixed in CL 2660.\n\nRelease/changelog mapping evidence:\n- CHANGELOG.md lines 41-52 name every removed spelling and replacement: REBAR_NO_SYNC -> REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off, COMPACT_THRESHOLD -> REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD, SCRATCH_BASE_DIR -> REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR, REBAR_ACLI_TIMEOUT -> REBAR_JIRA_CLI_TIMEOUT, RECONCILER_ABSENT_GET_BUDGET -> REBAR_RECONCILER_DELETION_PROBE_LIMIT, REBAR_ID_GUARD_MODE=warn -> REBAR_UNSAFE_ID_GUARD_BYPASS=true, REBAR_VERIFY_OVERLAP_ENABLED -> REBAR_VERIFY_SUGGEST_DUPLICATE_TICKETS, verify.overlap_enabled -> verify.suggest_duplicate_tickets.\n- docs/release-notes.md lines 11-29 publish the same ADR 0116 mapping table and call out the semantic migrations.\n\nLive-doc canonical evidence:\n- docs/config.md lines 156, 184, 213, 240, 348, 355, 360 now show only canonical env/config spellings in live examples.\n- docs/config.md lines 850-853 replace permanent-alias prose with ADR 0116 canonical-only guidance.\n- docs/bash-migration.md lines 25-28 now names only fetch and --no-pull opt-out.\n- docs/concurrency.md lines 840-845 now names REBAR_SYNC_PULL=off and --no-pull, not REBAR_NO_SYNC as a live alias.\n\nCensus evidence:\nA repo-wide census of the eight retired spellings was run after edits. Remaining matches are classified as: explicit migration docs in CHANGELOG.md/docs/release-notes.md; ADR/history in docs/adr/0116 and docs/adr/0086 / experiment fixtures; regression tests and tombstone/removal tests under tests/unit; generated config_surface canonical names where COMPACT_THRESHOLD/SCRATCH_BASE_DIR are substrings of REBAR_COMPACT_THRESHOLD/REBAR_SCRATCH_BASE_DIR; and .rebar/usage.jsonl LLM telemetry. No live guidance in docs/config.md, docs/env-vars.md, docs/config-reference.md, docs/bash-migration.md, or docs/concurrency.md presents retired names as aliases.\n\nGate evidence:\n- RED oracle: session artifact oracle_1a63_docs.py failed on current main because docs/config.md still contained live alias guidance.\n- GREEN oracle: same oracle passed after edits.\n- Mutation teeth: sandboxed mutation reintroduced REBAR_NO_SYNC live-alias text in docs/config.md; oracle failed, then passed after restoration.\n- Targeted tests: pytest tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py => 34 passed.\n- make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS.\n- Full local make test: baseline hit the documented macOS repo-isolation artifact; rerun with requested deselects then hit unrelated host gate-congestion failures while other sessions held plan-review slots. Gerrit Verified subsequently passed the full CI gate.\n- Gerrit CL 2660: Verified+1, LLM-Review+1, unresolved comments 0, submitted/merged.\n","timestamp":1788587259479691001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788421647151960001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1985bb1f-f6d0-469f-99e3-4b08409ec8f4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7370-0274-9f80-437d"},{"link_uuid":"68fb3c54-7f99-4097-aaaf-852daf32dc8d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8c99-9deb-58ca-4461"},{"link_uuid":"e3f4b610-ec45-4f43-853d-f1072a4906ef","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cf9c-a159-aa42-453e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0116 authorized clean pre-1.0 removal of eight old env/config spellings after runtime work landed. Upstream `7370-0274-9f80-437d` has landed on current `origin/main` (5ae93de838af) and already removed the active code aliases. Sibling `038d` was found obsolete because that landed change removed all eight aliases from code. This ticket publishes the remaining documentation/changelog surface so operators see canonical spellings and the migration mapping instead of live-alias guidance.\n\n## Current-main validity assessment\n\nOn current `origin/main`, `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/api-stability.md`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`, and `tests/golden/config_surface.json` are already regenerated/aligned/canonical for the removed aliases and should be validated, not hand-edited. Remaining gaps are hand-authored narrative/release surfaces and one env-registry regression expectation:\n\n- `docs/config.md` still presents the eight names as permanent/live aliases in example comments and Back-compat prose.\n- `docs/bash-migration.md` and `docs/concurrency.md` still mention `REBAR_NO_SYNC` as a live opt-out alias.\n- `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` need a release/changelog entry that names every removed spelling and canonical replacement; existing older release-note statements that say the aliases are still honored must be corrected as historical release notes.\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py` already retains an explicit absent-from-generated-docs expectation for all seven removed env spellings; keep it green as validation evidence.\n\n## Approach\n\nUpdate only the recorded file-impact paths. Regenerate generated surfaces only through their sanctioned generator if drift appears; otherwise leave already-regenerated generated files untouched and prove drift tests pass. Directly edit hand-authored docs/release notes to replace live-alias guidance with canonical-only configuration guidance and explicit ADR 0116 migration text. Run a full string census across the eight retired spellings and classify remaining occurrences as intentional tests, ADR/history, or migration documentation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/env-vars.md`, `docs/config.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`, `docs/bash-migration.md`, `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/api-stability.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`\n- `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`, `tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`, and `tests/golden/config_surface.json`\n- sanctioned generators only if those generated/golden surfaces drift\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED-first documentation oracle: a complete-population census/check that fails while live-alias guidance remains and while the changelog/release notes lack all eight ADR 0116 mappings.\n- Targeted generated-surface checks: `pytest tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py`.\n- Full local gates required for this ticket: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` (with only documented local macOS deselections if needed).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Live documentation and examples use only canonical spellings for the eight removed env/config names.\n- [x] Generated env/config reference surfaces and their tests are regenerated or verified so they no longer present the old names as live aliases.\n- [x] Release/changelog documentation names every removal and its canonical replacement.\n- [x] A full string census of the eight removed spellings leaves only intentional tombstones, the new ADR, explicit migration documentation, regression tests, or clearly historical references.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"remove live alias rows from generated env docs"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"replace live alias guidance with canonical-only text"},{"path":"docs/config-reference.md","reason":"remove verify.overlap_enabled alias documentation"},{"path":"docs/bash-migration.md","reason":"remove live REBAR_NO_SYNC alias guidance"},{"path":"docs/concurrency.md","reason":"remove live REBAR_NO_SYNC alias guidance"},{"path":"docs/api-stability.md","reason":"align published stability guidance with the ADR"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"record the alias removals and replacements"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"record the alias removals and replacements"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py","reason":"update env-registry expectations after alias retirement"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_surface_golden.py","reason":"update config-surface golden expectations"},{"path":"tests/golden/config_surface.json","reason":"regenerate the config-surface golden without verify.overlap_enabled"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","7370-0274-9f80-437d"],["parent","038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5"],["relates_to","8c99-9deb-58ca-4461"],["relates_to","cf9c-a159-aa42-453e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"038d-f5ff-b371-4ba5","parent_status_uuid":"4ada1d4a-a133-4d64-afd8-126a57600b74","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","config","breaking-change","compatibility"],"ticket_id":"1a63-056e-98b9-4ab7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Publish canonical config removal docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["68fb3c54-7f99-4097-aaaf-852daf32dc8d","b84aecee-4f2f-4870-9989-06b8c20c144d","c4712f64-6c6a-4f6b-a42d-bd3ba707437d","41fc8dd5-d4db-4213-8440-4d139ab8ea30","1e4d4218-8fba-4502-9022-edfb3de67900","826cf50d-df75-4766-b949-622f739e5aa1","f1aba4f3-ad43-4abf-aab0-6837fdcf08a5","e3f4b610-ec45-4f43-853d-f1072a4906ef","9dd21d3c-b1e1-46ee-8b08-1c1d02569b9c","36bb12df-f19d-4490-ad62-70d9358191ee","9f84e2a2-3d11-4a06-b47c-79564b295415","4ada1d4a-a133-4d64-afd8-126a57600b74","04f81081-4fd4-4ccd-93e1-81a2f7c9e224"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","even